    "summary": "Epic Dark Star suite, inspired Garcia solos and tight band jams",
    "blurb": "The show delivers an explosive Dark Star > Eyes Of The World > Half‑Step suite backed by fiery Jerry Garcia solos. China Cat Sunflower into I Know You Rider and a soaring Playing In The Band round out strong first‑set momentum, while the second set caps with tight Not Fade Away > Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad transitions. Overall soundboard clarity captures the band’s high energy despite an over‑prominent ride cymbal.",
    "review": "On February 26, 1973 at Pershing Municipal Auditorium in Lincoln, NE, the Dead turned a typical winter night into a landmark performance. From the opening “The Promised Land” through a marathon first set that built momentum with classics like “China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider,” the band kept the energy high, culminating in an inspired “Playing In The Band.” The second set is where the show truly shines: after a brief stumble on “Tennessee Jed” (Phil missed a couple of cues but quickly recovered), they launch into a monumental “Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → Mississippi Half‑Step Uptown Toodeloo,” with Jerry’s solos described as “extremely inspired.” Highlights continue with “Greatest Story Ever Told,” and the set closes with a seamless “Not Fade Away → Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad” medley. The Kaplan soundboard capture is generally clear and powerful, rendering the band’s dynamics vivid—though Billy’s ride cymbal sits forward in the mix at times. For anyone looking to hear this high‑octane early‑’70s Dead, this recording offers a crystal‑clear window into one of their most exhilarating February shows.",
